Ukrainian forces destroy over 4,700 Russian aerial targets in September, including eight Zircon missiles
Ukrinform
Ukraine's Defense Forces destroyed more than 4,700 aerial targets in September, including eight Iskander-M/KN-23 ballistic missiles and eight Zircon anti-ship missiles.
According to Ukrinform, the Ukrainian Air Force Command reported this on Facebook.
In addition, Ukraine's Defense Forces neutralized more than 48,000 tactical-level drones in September.
The aerial targets destroyed included:
- 24 Kh-101 cruise missiles;
- 8 Iskander-M/KN-23 ballistic missiles;
- 12 Kalibr cruise missiles
- 6 Kh-59/69 guided air-to-surface missiles;
- 6 Iskander-K cruise missiles;
- 8 Zircon anti-ship missiles;
- 86 S8000 Banderol small cruise missiles;
- 2,722 Shahed-131/136-type attack drones;
- 1,935 Shahed-238-type attack drones;
- 1,009 reconnaissance drones and 719 Lancet drones.
In August, the Air Force conducted more than 1,600 aircraft sorties, including around 1,300 sorties to provide fighter cover and more than 250 for strikes and air support for troops.
